      "raw_html": "<div class=\"question\" id=\"question-132546\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">3.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/3353#16589\">Computing Probabilities With Exponential Random Variables on a Bounded Interval</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"132546\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>Vehicles arrive at a crossing continuously in time, independently, and at a constant average rate of one every <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"31\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> seconds. Determine the probability that the next vehicle will arrive at the crossing within the next <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"32\" jax=\"CHTML\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\" tabindex=\"0\"><mjx-math aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml display=\"inline\" unselectable=\"on\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> seconds. Round your answer to four decimal places. </p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyEasy\">E</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Tue, Oct 13th @ 12:31 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 0:16</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>"
